      "equivalence": {
        "scope": "Kernel local operator semantics on executed refreshes; the full composition is deliberately lossy through Cache.",
        "method_argument": "On each complete denoiser refresh, the Kernel still computes the full RMS normalization of all 2240 Q/K channels using FP32 sum-square/C, original epsilon and weights, original BF16 normalization cast before ReLU, all even 112-channel heads and the original RoPE pair/frequency indices. Rotary results round to original BF16 before exact widening to FP32 for the original contractions. Full nonrotated features, denominator epsilon 1e-15, FP32 contractions, projections, cross-attention, FFN and residuals are unchanged. There is no Kernel approximation, sparsity, rank reduction, changed logical model work or lower precision. EasyCache is a separately declared lossy full-denoiser approximation: native latent relative-change prediction with online full-refresh output/input gain, complete output-minus-input vector, threshold 0.02, eligible middle steps 24 through 33 and at most one consecutive hit per isolated CFG branch. Its dense refresh closure contains the Kernel operator. The actual composition refreshed 90 and reused 10 calls on each prompt, measured anew because Kernel numerical movement can affect adaptive decisions. Original sampler, 50 steps, 100 global logical calls, BF16 transformer/FP32 VAE and world size 1 topology are preserved. Full DiT traversal observations remain unavailable and are not inferred from logical calls. Kernel correctness is a mathematical/source argument without output-difference or LPIPS gating of the Kernel component.",
